## Public API

Choose **closed**, **compound**, or **compound + shorthand** per component.

| Model | Use when | Public API | Barrel (`index.ts`) |
| ----- | -------- | ---------- | ------------------- |
| **Closed** | Single props surface; no subpart composition | `Foo` | `export * from "./foo"` |
| **Compound** | Consumer composes subparts | `Foo.Root`, `Foo.Title`, … | `Object.assign(FooRoot, { … })` |
| **Shorthand** | Repetitive composition wrapper | `FooShorthand` or root preset (`items`, `title`) | Attached via `Object.assign` on compound barrel |

**Shorthand when:**

1. **Layout blocks** — fixed slots (title / description / action regions)
2. **Selection lists** — data → options UI (`items` on the root or shorthand)
3. **Modal headers** — single canonical path: `Foo.Header` with `title` / `description`

**Shorthand not needed:** structural layout compounds, freeform markup lists, leaf primitives.

### Do

**Compound:**

- Name internally `{Name}Root`, `{Name}Item`, …; set `displayName`: root `"Foo.Root"` when a dedicated shorthand export exists, otherwise `"Foo"`; subparts `"Foo.Part"`.
- Implement compound parts first; shorthand composes them — never the reverse.
- Export via `Object.assign(FooShorthand, { Root, Item, Trigger, … })` when shorthand exists; otherwise `Object.assign(FooRoot, { … })`.
- Public surface is `Foo.Root` / `Foo.Part` only. Flat `FooPart` barrel re-exports are forbidden; do not ship a dual compound + flat surface.
- Detached presets (flat `FooField`) must attach on the namespace as `Foo.Field` (via `Object.assign` on the compound / shorthand object). No parallel flat compat export.
- Utils, hooks, and variants may remain named exports outside the namespace.
- `parameters.docs.api` must match the real barrel surface (`compound` / `compound-shorthand` only when the barrel is a true `Foo.Root` / `Foo.Part` namespace).

**Shorthand:**

- Name dedicated shorthand `FooShorthand` (not `FooClosed`); attach via `Object.assign(FooShorthand, { Root, Title, … })`.
- Type shorthand props with `Omit<FooRootProps, "children">` — no `children` on the default export.
- Prefer `<Foo title="…" />` over `<Foo.Root><Foo.Title>…</Foo.Title></Foo.Root>` when preset props are enough.
- Composition uses `Foo.Root` only when flexibility is required (`asChild`, custom markup, slot order); never nest `Foo.Title` / `Foo.Description` under `<Foo>`.
- Root preset shorthand (`items`, `title`) on `{Name}Root` only when the pattern is thin and there is no dedicated `FooShorthand`.
- One canonical shorthand path per concern — do not duplicate on both `Root` and `Header` / `Content`.

**Closed:**

- Export a single function with convenience props and DOM sub-element `*Props` bags (content/behavior — not styling).
- Export `{name}Variants` when part of the public API — see [Styling](#styling).
- Export via `export * from "./foo"` (shared package barrel only).

**Barrel (both):**

- Re-export types, hooks, or `RootProvider` only when part of the public API.
- Prefer owner `*Props` (`FooRootProps`, `FooCloseProps`) when wrapping or typing workspace components. Do not use `ComponentProps<typeof Foo>` / `ComponentProps<typeof Foo.Part>` for that — reserve `ComponentProps` for Ark/DOM primitives and third-party components that do not export props.

### Do not

- Do not ship two unrelated API models. Shorthand wraps compound — it is not a separate closed model.
- Dual API (compound + shorthand) is per-component only — not every component needs both.
- Do not use `<Foo>` as a composition root when `FooShorthand` is the default export — use `<Foo.Root>`.
- Do not pass `children` to shorthand exports for manual subpart layout.
- Do not fall back to `children` in shorthand (`description ?? children`, `title ?? children`).
- Do not keep placeholder `tv()` slots (`""`, `[]`) to generate `classNames` keys.
- Do not type wrappers with `ComponentProps<typeof Foo.Part>` when that part exports `FooPartProps` / `FooCloseProps` (owner props).
- Do not re-export flat `FooPart` siblings from the barrel beside the `Foo.Root` / `Foo.Part` namespace.
- Do not leave a detached flat `FooField` export beside `Foo.Field`.

**Pattern guide:**

| Pattern | Use |
| ------- | --- |
| **Compound + headless** | `{Name}Root` + subparts; headless primitive; `Object.assign` barrel |
| **Compound + shorthand** | Compound = source of truth; `FooShorthand` or root preset for common cases |
| **Compound barrel** | `Object.assign(FooRoot, { Item, Trigger, … })` in `index.ts` |
| **Closed + multi-slot `tv()`** | Single export; `slots:` variants; sub-element `classNames` bags |
| **Closed + behavior** | Single export; convenience props; minimal `tv()` or `base:` only |
| **Closed + primitive wrapper** | Thin styled layer over one headless part |
| **Composition layer** | Composes other package exports (e.g. `@pisagor/react/*`); no new primitive |

**Example:**

```ts
export const Foo = Object.assign(FooShorthand, {
  Root: FooRoot,
  Title: FooTitle,
  Description: FooDescription,
  Action: FooAction,
});
```

```tsx
// Shorthand (default export) — not a composition root
<Foo title="Heads up!" description="…" />

// Composition — always Foo.Root
<Foo.Root>
  <Foo.Title>Heads up!</Foo.Title>
  <Foo.Description>…</Foo.Description>
</Foo.Root>
```

In `FooShorthand` (and similar layout compose returns), leave a **blank line between each top-level slot** sibling in JSX. Nested containers group their own children without extra spacing.

