## File regions

Every `<name>.tsx` file uses `#region` blocks in this order. Skip regions that do not apply; never reorder.

| Order | Region | When |
| ----- | ------ | ---- |
| 1 | `Variants` | Component uses `tv()` — see [Styling](#styling) |
| 2 | `Types` | Props, variant types, context types, item interfaces |
| 3 | `Context` | Shared React context for compound components only |
| 4 | `Hooks` | File-local hooks not exported from `index.ts` |
| 5 | `Component` / `Components` | All component functions — see below |

### Do

- Use **`#region Component`** (singular) when the file exports **one** component function.
- Use **`#region Components`** (plural) when the file exports **two or more** component functions.
- Place `Variants` before `Types` so variant types can reference `{name}Variants`.
- Start at `Types` → `Component(s)` when there is no `tv()`.
- Follow [react.mdc → Component body order](../styleguides/react.mdc#component-body-order) inside each component function.

### Do not

- Do not add an `Exports` region — public API belongs in `index.ts`.

**Note:** Types region order is file-level type declaration order — not the same as [react.mdc → Props order](../styleguides/react.mdc#props-order) field groups.

Inside `Types`, when all apply: sub-element prop types → `{Name}ClassNames` → `{Name}VariantProps` → root props → public interface → preset interfaces (`AccordionItem`, …).

