## Types

Follow [React Style Guide](../styleguides/react.mdc) for naming and [props field order](../styleguides/react.mdc#props-order). On the public props interface, add **sub-element bags** after styling props.

### Do

- Extend `ComponentProps<typeof Primitive.Part>` or `ComponentProps<typeof ark.div>`.
- Use `export interface FooProps` when props are part of the public API.
- Combine with `interface FooProps extends FooRootProps, FooVariantProps`.
- Use `Omit<…>` when a convenience prop conflicts with DOM attributes.
- Add `VariantProps<typeof fooVariants>` + JSDoc `@default` matching `defaultVariants` from [Styling](#styling).
- Type sub-element bags as `titleProps?: Omit<TitleProps, "children" | "className">`.

| `Omit` usage | Valid | Invalid |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Convenience prop conflicts with primitive prop | `type SelectRootProps = Omit<ArkSelectRootProps<Item>, "collection" \| "onValueChange">;` | `type SelectRootProps = ArkSelectRootProps<Item>;` + re-declare `onValueChange` with a different signature |
| Sub-element prop bags keep ownership of render/styling | `contentProps?: Omit<TooltipContentProps, "children" \| "className">` | `contentProps?: TooltipContentProps` (allows overriding `children`/`className`) |
| Preserve primitive contracts by default | `interface DialogBodyProps extends ComponentProps<typeof ark.div> {}` (no `Omit` needed) | `type DialogBodyProps = Omit<ComponentProps<typeof ark.div>, "role">` without an explicit conflict |

### Do not

- Do not route styling through `*Props` bags — use `classNames` on multi-slot components only; single-element components use `className`.
- Do not type `classNames` as `VariantClassNames<typeof fooVariants> & { … }` — use `VariantClassNames` only.
- `titleProps` / `contentProps` on shorthand APIs: behavior escape-hatches only (`Omit<…, "children" | "className">`).

