## Headless wrapper

Behavior lives in the headless primitive — the styled layer adds visuals only.

### Do

- Type each part per [Types](#types).
- Follow [react.mdc → Props order](../styleguides/react.mdc#props-order) for JSX attribute order on each element. On **plain** nodes (`ark.div`, native tags) add `data-scope` / `data-part`; do **not** set them on machine-backed `<XPrimitive.Part>` nodes — Zag already emits them.
- Alias imports to avoid name clashes (`Accordion as AccordionPrimitive`).
- Use a factory element (`ark.div`) only when there is no headless part for that DOM node.
- Forward `asChild` and portal props unchanged.
- Set overlay defaults when supported: `lazyMount = true`, `unmountOnExit = true`.

### Do not

- Do not reimplement keyboard handling, focus trap, or open/close logic.

---

## Styling

- **`cn()`:** one logical concern per string; `className` last.
- Use **semantic tokens** (`bg-muted`, `text-muted-foreground`).
- **`tv()`:** export `{name}Variants`; use `slots:` for multi-part DOM, `base:` for single element; set `defaultVariants` and mirror in destructuring.
- **`base:`** — single DOM node in the file (or dedicated export e.g. `inputRootVariants`).
- **`slots:`** — only parts with real default styles; every slot key must have non-empty class strings.
- **Do not** add placeholder slots (`""`, `[]`) to generate `classNames` keys — remove the slot and override per [Override without a slot](#override-without-a-slot).
- When a multi-export file names list chrome, use part names (`list`, not `base`) — e.g. `tabsListVariants` uses `slots.list`.
- Split `tv()` when reuse needs a shared root shell (`inputRootVariants`) separate from optional slots (`inputVariants.clearableRoot`).
- **Root** always accepts **`className`** — never `rootClassName`.
- **Single-element components:** merge with `cn(fooVariants({ … }), className)` — no `classNames` prop.
- **Multi-slot components:** merge with `cn(slots.part({ … }), className, classNames?.part)`; type **`classNames`** as `VariantClassNames<typeof {name}Variants>`.
- **Root with both** `className` and `classNames?.root`: `cn(slots.root({ … }), className, classNames?.root)`.
- Apply **motion & focus:** `motion-reduce:transition-none!`; `outline-hidden` + `focus-visible:ring-[3px] focus-visible:ring-ring/32`; style `disabled:`, `data-disabled:`, `aria-disabled:` consistently.
- On **plain** styled nodes, set **`data-scope="{name}"`** and **`data-part="{part}"`** (root uses `data-part="root"`). On machine-backed parts, omit both — Ark/Zag already emit `data-scope` / `data-part`. Never override those attributes on a primitive part (Zag queries the DOM through them).
- Mirror variant props on root when useful (`data-variant`, `data-size`, `data-shape`).

### Override without a slot

When a part has no `tv()` slot by design:

1. **Compound part** — pass `className` on `{Name}Part` directly.
2. **`asChild`** — merge classes onto the child element.
3. **Remove** erroneous empty slots from `tv()` — do not keep placeholders for typing.
4. **Do not** add `*Props.className` or per-part styling bags.

